backport: use CJK fonts for half/fullwidth forms and punctuation (bug 709678)

BACKPORT of upstream mupdf 27d8576c07ca578dd32b270934ee262b67dba9ae, not a
change of ours. Drop it when the vendored mupdf moves past that commit - it is
on mupdf master but not in 1.28.2.

https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709678

Halfwidth/fullwidth forms (U+FF01-FFEE, including the fullwidth comma) and CJK
punctuation (U+3000-303F) are not in the Han/Hiragana/Hangul scripts, so the
appearance generator treated them as unencodable and took the rich HTML path,
which embeds a fallback font. Treat them as Han so they stay on the simple
CJK path.

Replaces our 0034-pdf-appearance-cjk-annotation-text rewrite for issue #6082.

Fixes https://github.com/sumatrapdfreader/sumatrapdf/issues/6082
---
diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
index 4cd48587e..eabdbd34e 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
@@ -1668,6 +1668,14 @@ add_required_fonts(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, pdf_obj *res_font,
 		case UCDN_SCRIPT_BOPOMOFO: add_bopomofo = 1; break;
 		case UCDN_SCRIPT_HAN: add_han = 1; break;
 		}
+
+		// halfwidth and fullwidth forms
+		if (c >= 0xff01 && c <= 0xffee)
+			add_han = 1;
+
+		// cjk symbols and punctuation
+		if (c >= 0x3000 && c <= 0x303f)
+			add_han = 1;
 	}
 
 	if (add_han)
@@ -1803,6 +1811,15 @@ static int next_text_walk(fz_context *ctx, struct text_walk_state *state)
 
 	state->n = fz_chartorune(&state->u, state->text);
 	script = ucdn_get_script(state->u);
+
+	// halfwidth and fullwidth forms
+	if (state->u >= 0xff01 && state->u <= 0xffee)
+		script = UCDN_SCRIPT_HAN;
+
+	// cjk symbols and punctuation
+	if (state->u >= 0x3000 && state->u <= 0x303f)
+		script = UCDN_SCRIPT_HAN;
+
 	if (script == UCDN_SCRIPT_COMMON || script == UCDN_SCRIPT_INHERITED)
 		script = state->last_script;
 	state->last_script = script;
@@ -2459,6 +2476,14 @@ static int text_needs_rich_layout(fz_context *ctx, const char *s)
 		)
 			continue;
 
+		// halfwidth and fullwidth forms
+		if (c >= 0xff01 && c <= 0xffee)
+			continue;
+
+		// cjk symbols and punctuation
+		if (c >= 0x3000 && c <= 0x303f)
+			continue;
+
 		return 1;
 	}
 	return 0;
